    902	### F1 — Per-bit polylog extraction — **PARTIALLY CLOSED (S146, mode E, B-grade refinement of E1.3)**
    903	**Question:** Find J such that the J-th bit of `p(n)` is computable in polylog *for fixed J independent of N*. E1.3 says bits 0..0.6N match `round(R^{-1}(n))`. So J = 0 is trivially polylog. What is the LARGEST J for which `bit_J(p(n))` is provably polylog?
    904	**Why this is unblocked:** The whole-number question is closed; the per-bit question has an obvious YES answer for small J and an unknown answer for medium J. The boundary is the research target.
    905	**First step:** Read `novel/carry_propagation_boundary.md`. Build a per-bit accuracy curve as a function of J for N up to 30.
